<title>USA: Hallwood says more than 328,000 shr tendered.</title>
<headline>Hallwood says more than 328,000 shr tendered.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hallwood Group Inc said Monday that its commission-free, self-tender offer for up to 300,000 shares of its common stock had expired and that preliminary results indicate more than 328,000 shares were tendered, making proration provisions of its offer document effective.</p>
<p>The company said it is reviewing the results and would disclose more information on the method of proration and the number of shares to be bought as soon as possible.</p>
</text>
